-- a family of measurements counts independent events exactly when it is injective on events: two
-- places in the family holding one event are one measurement counted twice. This is the hypothesis
-- every statistic over an aggregate needs and no corpus states.
Distinct : (I : Type 0) → (V : Type 0) → (I → Measured V) → Type 0
Distinct I V f = (i : I) → (j : I) → meas-event V (f i) ≡ meas-event V (f j) → i ≡ j
